GNU Global's programs, carried in NppGTags' package rather than installed where they were configured,
find what is beside them, as Global's Windows build does: 'bindir' is the running program's folder and
'datadir' the share folder beside it (libutil/conf.c), the pygments parser's script is found in that
'datadir' (plugin-factory/pygments-parser.c), and the script asks the gtags beside it for the ctags
program (plugin-factory/pygments_parser.py.in). Applied by gnu-global.cmake to Global 6.6.12.

